Exact-pin `tokenizers` so the late `--pre` transformers install cannot pull the
release candidate SGLang explicitly pins away from.

SGLang v0.5.19 added this to python/pyproject.toml:

  "tokenizers==0.22.2", # 0.23.0rc0 is incompatible with transformers' CLIPTokenizer.

The image does NOT honour that pin, and the 0.5.19-sm121 image built 2026-09-11
shipped `tokenizers 0.23.0-rc0`. Two independent reasons, either one is enough:

  * stages/missing_deps.py only checks PRESENCE of a dependency, never its
    version, so anything an earlier step already installed stays where it is and
    a new upstream pin never moves it.
  * the late transformers step installs with `--pre`
    (`uv pip install -U transformers==${TRANSFORMERS_VERSION} --pre`), and
    transformers 5.12.1 itself only requires `tokenizers>=0.22.0,<=0.23.0`, so
    with prereleases allowed pip is free to resolve the RC inside that range.

What upstream says breaks is transformers' CLIPTokenizer, i.e. the CLIP-based
multimodal/diffusion tokenizer paths, not the NVFP4 text models this cluster
mostly serves. NOT independently reproduced here (a synthetic CLIP vocab test in
the built image was inconclusive), so this is upstream's assertion plus our
observed version mismatch, which is reason enough to match the pin rather than
find out in production.

Pinned here rather than by dropping `--pre` from the transformers step: that flag
is upstream's own and a future recipe may legitimately want a prerelease
transformers. This way the tokenizers version is an explicit, visible build knob
and the transformers step keeps its upstream semantics.

  ARG TOKENIZERS_VERSION=""   # empty = leave tokenizers as resolved (older recipes)
  TOKENIZERS_VERSION=0.22.2   # in sglang-0.5.19-sm121.recipe and later

Mechanism mirrors dockerfile-hf-hub-floor.patch: an `ARG` + gated `uv pip
install` RUN in the builder stage, before the dist-packages split, so it is
carried into the runtime stage. It is an EXACT pin (==), not a floor, because
that is what upstream pins and the next tokenizers release may well be the
incompatible one. Installed with `--no-deps`, which is the one deliberate
difference from the hub floor: tokenizers' only runtime dependency is
`huggingface_hub>=0.16.4`, already satisfied several major versions over by the
floor installed immediately above, so --no-deps makes this step provably unable
to move hub. Both variants were tried against the 2026-09-11 image: with deps uv
also bumped filelock, with --no-deps exactly one package changes.

VALIDATED 2026-09-11 inside the built 0.5.19-sm121 image (no rebuild needed):
`uv pip install --no-deps tokenizers==0.22.2` downgrades 0.23.0rc0 -> 0.22.2,
after which transformers 5.12.1 still imports, `from transformers import
CLIPTokenizer` works, huggingface_hub stays 1.31.0, and sglang plus
srt.entrypoints.http_server still import. So the pin is safe to bake in; what it
FIXES is upstream's claim, not something reproduced here.

PLACEMENT: LAST in the builder stage, immediately before the `# Break up
dist-packages ...` split and therefore AFTER the hf-hub floor, so no later
resolve can move tokenizers again. The hunk is TRAILING-CONTEXT-ONLY (anchored
on the upstream split block), so it applies regardless of which optional
dockerfile-*.patch steps ran before it, and it must be applied LAST in
apply_patches(), after dockerfile-hf-hub-floor.patch.

Remove once SGLang's own pin is honoured by the resolve (i.e. once missing_deps
compares versions, or the transformers step stops using --pre).

Apply to: container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly in the local clone of
scitrera/cuda-containers.

--- a/container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
+++ b/container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly
@@ -498,3 +498,28 @@
+# dgxarley: exact-pin tokenizers. SGLang v0.5.19 added `tokenizers==0.22.2` to
+# its pyproject with the note that 0.23.0rc0 is incompatible with transformers'
+# CLIPTokenizer, but this image does not honour that pin: missing_deps.py only
+# checks PRESENCE (never version), and the late transformers step above installs
+# with `--pre`, which lets pip satisfy transformers' own `tokenizers>=0.22.0,
+# <=0.23.0` range with the RELEASE CANDIDATE. The 0.5.19-sm121 image built
+# 2026-09-11 shipped tokenizers 0.23.0-rc0 for exactly that reason. Pinned here
+# rather than by dropping `--pre` from the transformers step, because that flag
+# is upstream's and some recipes may want a prerelease transformers; and pinned
+# LAST in the builder stage so no earlier resolve can move it again. Gated by
+# TOKENIZERS_VERSION (empty = leave tokenizers as resolved, so every older
+# recipe is byte-identical). --no-deps, UNLIKE the hub floor above: this is an
+# exact downgrade of one leaf package whose only runtime dependency is
+# huggingface_hub>=0.16.4, already satisfied many times over by the floor
+# installed directly above, so --no-deps makes this step provably unable to
+# disturb it. Verified in the 2026-09-11 image: with deps it also moved filelock,
+# with --no-deps exactly one package changes and hub stays put.
+ARG TOKENIZERS_VERSION=""
+RUN --mount=type=cache,id=uv-cache,target=/root/.cache/uv \
+    if [ -n "$TOKENIZERS_VERSION" ]; then \
+        echo "=== Pinning tokenizers==${TOKENIZERS_VERSION} (CLIPTokenizer vs 0.23.0rc0) ==="; \
+        uv pip install --no-deps "tokenizers==${TOKENIZERS_VERSION}"; \
+        python3 -c "import tokenizers; print('tokenizers', tokenizers.__version__)"; \
+    fi
+
 # Break up dist-packages into smaller layers to avoid hitting Docker layer size limits
 COPY stages/directory_split2.sh /opt/directory_split2.sh
 RUN chmod +x /opt/directory_split2.sh && \
